      "reason": "Dialogue supports the decision that the remote will have two basic functions (input channel/volume; location function) and that a radio-based signaling method to locate the remote is preferred over IR, with a receiver output (buzzer/light) and button-based activation mentioned. The scope matches the advertised text across multiple lines in ES2011b observed dialogue.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.13",
          "quote": "Um so I think we need two basic functions which is just the basic remote functions ,"
        },
        {
          "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.14",
          "quote": "the user can input a channel or volume setting and it will be output to the T_V_ ."
        },
        {
          "da_id": "ES2011b.B.dialog-act.dharshi.15",
          "quote": "And also we talked about um a location function where maybe you could press a button on the T_V_ and it would send sort of signal to the remote where it would beep or flash or vibrate or whatever to tell you where the remote is ."
